# Go conventions

See [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).

## Package

- Single root package `forecast`
- Module: `github.com/eduard-kolotushin/timeseries-forecast`
- Go 1.26+

## API

- Fit functions return `Fitted`
- `Forecast(h)` returns a new `timeseries.Series[float64]`
- `ForecastInterval(h, level)` returns lower and upper series
- `ForecastRange(from, to)` / `ForecastIntervalRange` emit grid points in `[from, to]`
- `SnapshotOf` / `Restore` persist fitted state, not the training series
- Do not mutate caller series
- Pre-size forecast slices to `h` or the window length

## Quality

- Table-driven tests next to code
- No drive-by refactors
- Fit and forecast stay linear-time (see performance.mdc)
